+### Declaring read-only probes
+
+`DRIVER_PROBES` declares the named commands the `run_probe` action may
+run: `name=command` entries separated by `;`, for example
+`DRIVER_PROBES="git_status=git status --porcelain; disk_free=df -h"`.
+A declared command is split exactly like `DRIVER_CLI_COMMAND`
+(whitespace tokenisation, quotes group, nothing expanded) and runs as
+an argv list with no shell; the action's `command` parameter only ever
+*names* an entry, so there is nothing for a caller to compose or inject.
+Declaring a probe asserts it is read-only — the driver cannot verify
+that, so declare check and status commands only. A malformed
+declaration fails settings load rather than being skipped.
+
